From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:36:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/21] Make captured methods recoverable without guessing

Correlate codeitem evidence to one complete DEX by method identity, require equal parsed spans, preserve conflicts as partial evidence, and let dexdump failures revoke usability.

Constraint: Codeitem backfill must happen in the Python host repair path without modifying raw captures.
Rejected: Runtime-side backfill | the requested delivery flow requires post-export Python repair
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: moderate
Directive: Keep future reconstruction unique, boundary-checked, conflict-free, and content-addressed.
Tested: 15 host repair tests; real Coolapk run backfilled 302 codeitems and passed dexdump on the reconstructed DEX
Not-tested: JADX validation was not run
Change-Id: I542aa2fadca9432fb331b3d07663e789d45eec13
